  "_type": "reference"
 },
 "body": [
  {
   "_key": "000000000001",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000000",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "A trip from Canada to Egypt is not a short weekend."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000003",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "ykkwocehtok6",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Flight time is long, the time difference is real, and where you go after arrival — "
    },
    {
     "_key": "7z0wweur2suf",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "gy934bg9e6gy"
     ],
     "text": "Cairo"
    },
    {
     "_key": "dby7doma1vif",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "vklz6wd7sqi5",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "k02e13fa6qgu"
     ],
     "text": "Giza"
    },
    {
     "_key": "o0s1f0wzvlfc",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "25ep454ejsfc",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "66erylso03et"
     ],
     "text": "Luxor"
    },
    {
     "_key": "oml1y6uzwps2",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "bn7uq24s5iec",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "ukch1gs6fc41"
     ],
     "text": "Aswan"
    },
    {
     "_key": "4ul2agen994b",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", the Red Sea — changes the trip's shape. So Egypt is less a country for \"find a cheap package and book\" and more a country where you decide the overall flow first."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "gy934bg9e6gy",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "k02e13fa6qgu",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "66erylso03et",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "ukch1gs6fc41",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000005",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000004",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For travellers coming from Canada, three things matter most. Choose a workable flight route. Don't get the season wrong. And give the trip enough days for the transfer time it takes."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000007",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000006",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "How to think about the flight route"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000009",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000008",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "EgyptAir operates a direct flight from Toronto Pearson to Cairo. For travellers near Toronto, it is the most legible doorway."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000000a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Canada is a large country. From Montreal, Vancouver, Calgary, or Ottawa, you'll compare European, Middle Eastern, or Toronto connections."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000000c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Common transfer points include Istanbul, Doha, Dubai, Frankfurt, London, and Paris. Which route is best is decided less by the airline name and more by the transfer time and the arrival hour. With a late-night Cairo arrival, treat day one as transfer only. Even an early arrival, packed with sightseeing, tires you."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000000f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000000e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For winter Canada departures, also factor in domestic and European connection delays. A slightly looser connection beats one cut too tight."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000011",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000010",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Visa and entry"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000013",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000012",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Canadian passport holders need a tourist visa for Egypt."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000015",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000014",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "A Canadian can apply for an e-visa in advance or obtain a 30-day tourist visa on arrival. The visa-on-arrival is generally paid in US-dollar cash; carrying dollars is the safe call."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000017",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000016",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Visa rules change. Before travelling, check Egypt's official e-visa site and Canadian government travel advice. Passport validity matters too — many airlines check that you have enough time remaining beyond the return date."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000019",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000018",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Egyptian-Canadians, dual nationals, and travellers with Egyptian birth records may be treated differently from ordinary tourists for entry and military-service considerations. If this applies, confirm with official sources before departure."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "When to go"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For Canada-to-Egypt trips, the easiest window is October to April."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000001f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000001e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In this period, Cairo, Giza, Luxor, and Aswan all walk well and the sites read clearly. December and January are comfortable but crowded and pricier. November, February, and March often balance weather and crowds."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000021",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000020",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Summer can look cheaper; the heat in upper Egypt is real. In Luxor and Aswan, daytime outdoor sightseeing is severe. A Red Sea resort trip works in summer; a real ancient-sites trip in summer needs careful thought."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000023",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000022",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Leaving Canada in winter, Egypt's February is a particularly good choice. You get away from the Canadian cold and find walkable temperatures for sightseeing."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000025",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000024",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "How many days"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000027",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000026",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "From Canada, aim for at least ten days, ideally twelve to fourteen."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000029",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000028",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Flying alone uses big chunks of time, so seven days pushes you to rush. To see Cairo–Giza, Luxor, and Aswan unhurried, ten is the practical floor. To add the Red Sea or the desert, twelve or more keeps the trip from breaking."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For a first trip: two or three nights in Cairo, two or three in Luxor, three to four for the Nile cruise or Aswan stay, two or three on the Red Sea at the end. That spread is workable."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "On a shorter trip, deepen Cairo and Luxor rather than adding destinations."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000002f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000002e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "A first itinerary"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000031",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000030",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For a first Egypt trip, the base is Cairo, Giza, Luxor, and Aswan."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000033",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "miq05uziw0io",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Cairo, see the Giza pyramids, the Grand Egyptian Museum, and Islamic Cairo or "
    },
    {
     "_key": "079kkh6j285t",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "b4nhvsufx8go"
     ],
     "text": "Coptic Cairo"
    },
    {
     "_key": "4xq0nxyn2y0t",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ". Giza and the museum sit in the same area and pair well; both carry heavy information, so give time."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "b4nhvsufx8go",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-63606",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000035",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "1deoxcxqsq5d",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Luxor, centre on east-bank Karnak and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "zdlerv9y4q5p",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "7rodbbk38iuf"
     ],
     "text": "Luxor Temple"
    },
    {
     "_key": "5e5swqyvv1zo",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " and on west-bank "
    },
    {
     "_key": "f6ej64ce0ng2",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "nruuhpx0ob9x"
     ],
     "text": "Valley of the Kings"
    },
    {
     "_key": "43xldwzrglbi",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", Hatshepsut, and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "k29q2f4u3tn4",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "v6m7wu57bp4u"
     ],
     "text": "Medinet Habu"
    },
    {
     "_key": "l2cfvkcoqxrz",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ". This is the core of an Egypt trip. Use at least two days rather than passing through."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "7rodbbk38iuf",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "nruuhpx0ob9x",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "v6m7wu57bp4u",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.madinat-habu-temple",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000037",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "hb9yboap4xxh",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Aswan, Philae, "
    },
    {
     "_key": "i2sfppge5gfp",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "lv6ktnl0geyd"
     ],
     "text": "the Nubian Museum"
    },
    {
     "_key": "4u6cjkrv3x0i",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", a felucca, and "
    },
    {
     "_key": "bxqd25g1z79f",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "mkjh5egxxho1"
     ],
     "text": "Abu Simbel"
    },
    {
     "_key": "6clixy3jtoem",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " if you can. Aswan is calmer than Luxor and fits naturally toward the end of the itinerary."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "lv6ktnl0geyd",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "guideArticle.aswan.the-nubian-museum",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "mkjh5egxxho1",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000039",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "tzwip7so33ty",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "If the Red Sea is in, the last stop is most natural. Choose "
    },
    {
     "_key": "ct4o77pi3j7u",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "6rnh6q4z91yk"
     ],
     "text": "Hurghada"
    },
    {
     "_key": "ta85ywohnvd2",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "_key": "fpxm3ru0p8xf",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "26oa8vc75qc2"
     ],
     "text": "El Gouna"
    },
    {
     "_key": "2klhlylzkfh4",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": ", Sharm el-Sheikh, or "
    },
    {
     "_key": "qdxkvcsoydaj",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [
      "krt22eylg2fq"
     ],
     "text": "Marsa Alam"
    },
    {
     "_key": "gitw6t1bg6ip",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": " by rest, diving, hotel atmosphere, and transfer route."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [
    {
     "_key": "6rnh6q4z91yk",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "26oa8vc75qc2",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58740",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    },
    {
     "_key": "krt22eylg2fq",
     "_type": "internalLink",
     "reference": {
      "_ref": "wp-page-58885",
      "_type": "reference"
     }
    }
   ],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In-country movement"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "In Egypt, how you move between Cairo, Luxor, Aswan, and the Red Sea matters."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000003f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000003e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Cairo to Luxor or Aswan: domestic flight saves the most time. Overnight train is an option for travellers who enjoy the transfer itself. On a short itinerary, flights protect the time at sites."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000041",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000040",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Luxor to Aswan: Nile cruise, dahabiya, road, train, or domestic flight. For a first trip, the cruise is the most legible. For a slow river-focused trip, a dahabiya is the candidate but needs days and budget."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000043",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000042",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "If the Red Sea is included, Hurghada connects easily to Luxor by road. Sharm and Marsa Alam often work better by air given the itinerary."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000045",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000044",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Money and payments"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000047",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000046",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Egypt's currency is the Egyptian pound."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000049",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000048",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Rather than converting Canadian dollars directly to Egyptian pounds in advance, ATMs in Egypt or exchanging from a major currency on the ground is usually practical. ATMs are available at airports, hotels, and major cities; many small payments don't take cards, so carry cash."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Build tipping into the plan. Guides, drivers, hotel staff, and cruise crew all come into it. Carry small notes to avoid scrambling on the ground."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Credit cards work at large hotels and some restaurants; in markets, small shops, and regional payments, cash is central."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000004f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000004e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Safety and travel advice"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000051",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000050",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The Canadian government publishes current travel advice for Egypt. Check before travelling."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000053",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000052",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "The main tourism routes — Cairo, Giza, Luxor, Aswan, and the Red Sea resorts — see many travellers. Sinai's interior, border areas, and desert routes carry attention that varies by period and area."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000055",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000054",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Travel insurance is essential. Choose a policy that includes medical, hospitalisation, emergency evacuation, and trip interruption. For a long-distance trip, coverage for connection delays and baggage delay also has meaning."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000057",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000056",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Practical notes for Canadian travellers"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000059",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000058",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Don't underestimate jet lag and travel fatigue."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005b",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005a",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Going to Giza the day after arrival is possible; with a late-night arrival, keep the morning light or push the first sightseeing to the afternoon. After a long-haul flight, Cairo traffic and the wide Giza plateau are heavier than they look."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005d",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005c",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Dress for both heat and culture. Sun cover at the sites, shoulders and knees covered at religious sites, resort wear for the Red Sea. A light long sleeve, hat, walking shoes, and a light jacket help."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "00000000005f",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "00000000005e",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Even in winter, mornings and evenings can be cold. Coming from Canada it feels warm, but Cairo and Luxor nights, the desert, and the boat deck want a layer."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000061",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000060",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Conclusion"
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "h2"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000063",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000062",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Travelling from Canada to Egypt, build a trip that matches the distance."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000065",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000064",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Going only for the pyramids is too short against the flight time. Set the doorway at Cairo and Giza, see the core of ancient Egypt at Luxor, feel the southern Nile at Aswan. With days, rest on the Red Sea. As a first trip, that is the most reasonable shape."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000067",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000066",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Egypt is worth the long flight."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000069",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000068",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "Its value is most visible when the itinerary doesn't rush."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  }
 ],
